---
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="h-install">
  <div class="section-head"><h2 id="h-install">How installing works</h2></div>
  <p class="intro">
    Most apps here are shell scripts that run on the router itself. You need SSH access, which every
    GL.iNet router has out of the box.
  </p>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <h3>Connect via SSH</h3>
      <p>Open a terminal and log in with your admin password. The default router address is 192.168.8.1.</p>
      <Terminal command="ssh root@192.168.8.1" label="your computer" prompt="$" />
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <h3>Run the installer</h3>
      <p>Press Install on any app. You get its command with a copy button, plus what to check before you run it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <h3>Follow the prompts</h3>
      <p>Most scripts ask before they change anything and explain how to undo it. Details are in each project's README.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3.5l9.5 16.5h-19z"></path><path d="M12 10v4.5"></path><path d="M12 17.3h.01"></path></svg>
    <p>
      These are community projects, not GL.iNet software, and GL.iNet support can't help with them. Read
      a script before you run it, keep a configuration backup, and expect a firmware update to undo some
      changes.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
